  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "f1-testing-md-gate-tier",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "pre-existing",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/references/testing.md:26",
      "summary": "The every-spec running-tests tier still says \"Project gate: run it one time on the final commit of a spec\" without saying who runs it. implementer.md:28 sends the implementer to that tier and line 33 then says never run the gate, so an implementer reading both meets a contradiction; joycraft-implement SKILL.md:59 (inline implementer path, e.g. hosts without an implementer agent file) sends the implementer to the same tier. Not per step, so Max's note is met, but spec 15 (which owns testing.md, criterion 3 only requires gateRuns there) should make the tier say the coordinator runs the gate at gate-plan points and workers run focused tests only."
    },
    {
      "id": "f2-commands-in-startup-output",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.agents/skills/joycraft-verify/SKILL.md:51",
      "summary": "\"the packet's `commands.focused`\" follows the spec's wording, but dispatch-start.mjs:221 returns `commands` in the startup output beside `packet`, not inside the packet file under .joycraft/local/packets/. implementer.md:18 says \"startup output's `commands`\". A reviewer that opens only the packet file will not find it; \"startup output's\" would be exact at no word cost."
    },
    {
      "id": "f3-scope-section-gate",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "pre-existing",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/runtime/queue-check.mjs:334",
      "summary": "gate-in-spec checks only acceptance bullets. A spec's \"Implementation and verification scope\" can still name the gate (this feature's own specs say \"gate `pnpm test && pnpm typecheck`\" there, e.g. 14-tier-text.md:29), and the template does not forbid it. With gateRuns: spec this is once per spec, not per step, so it is not a contradiction; consider extending the decompose sentence or the check to that section."
    },
    {
      "id": "f4-entry-rule",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "pre-existing",
      "at": "AGENTS.md:15",
      "summary": "This project's own Rules line \"Run `pnpm test && pnpm typecheck` before committing\" still tells every agent to run the gate per commit. It is an owner rule, handled by spec 16's attended gate-rule decision, not by spec 14; listed so the feature-level review confirms Max decides it."
    },
    {
      "id": "f5-test-pins-sentences",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "tests/text-spec-tier.test.ts:41",
      "summary": "The spec-14 tests pin whole sentences (exact template/decompose sentence, implementer sentence, setup sentence), so any rewording breaks them. Acceptable for text specs, but shorter key-phrase assertions would be less brittle."
    }
  ]
